  "strategy": "To minimize the evaluation function effectively, we employ a differential evolution algorithm on a logarithmic scale of the sequence coefficients, combined with coordinate descent refinement. We start from a random initial sequence normalized to have sum=1, then use a terminator min_score=1.5027 as both upper bound on the minimization function. \n\nKey steps:\n1. Generate random sequence normalized to sum=1\n2. Use logarithmic scale for DE to avoid numerical instability\n3. Perform coordinate descent to minimize the maximum convolution value\n4. Compare the obtained value with the quote min_score and stop if better\n5. Explicitly maintain a running best sequence \n\nHere's the detailed approach:\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.fft import rfft, irfft\n\ndef evaluate_sequence(seq):\n    if not isinstance(seq, list):\n        return np.inf\n    if len(seq) == 0:\n        return np.inf\n    for x in seq:\n        if isinstance(x, bool) or not isinstance(x, (int, float)):\n            return np.inf\n        if np.isnan(x) or np.isinf(x):\n            return np.inf\n    clean_seq = [float(x) for x in seq]\n    clean_seq = [max(0, x) for x in clean_seq]\n    clean_seq = [min(1000.0, x) for x in clean_seq]\n    n = len(clean_seq)\n    conv = np.convolve(clean_seq, clean_seq)\n    max_b = max(conv)\n    sum_a = sum(clean_seq)\n    return (2 * n * max_b) / (sum_a ** 2) if sum_a > 0.01 else np.inf\n\ndef propose_candidate(parent=None, seed=42, max_n=None, time_budget=1500):\n    global height_sequence_1\n    start_time = time.time()\n    end_time = start_time + time_budget\n    \n    # Normalize parent sequence if provided or use random initialization\n    if parent is not None:\n        if isinstance(parent, str) and parent == \"load\":\n            try:\n                # In a real implementation, this would load the parent sequence\n                parent_arr = np.ones(800) / 800  # Fallback initialization for demonstration\n            except Exception as e:\n                pass\n    else:\n        np.random.seed(seed)\n        a_init = random_init(seed, max_n) if max_n is not None else np.ones(800) / 800\n    \n    seq = np.maximum(a_init, 0) * scale_factor  # Scale coefficients logarithmically\n    best_seq = seq.copy()\n    best_score = evaluate_sequence(best_seq)\n    \n    while best_score >= 1.503 and time.time() < end_time:\n        # Apply coordinate descent\n        n_coords = len(best_seq)\n        inv = np.log(np.array(best_seq)) * descent_factor\n        \n        # Calculate initial convolution to determine max_b\n        conv_val = np.convolve(seq, seq)\n        max_b = np.max(conv_val)\n        sum_a = np.sum(seq)\n        \n        # Use DE to find new candidate sequence\n        bounds = np.log([-1 + tolerance, tolerance_bound])  # Logarithmic bounds\n        new_seq = differential_evolution(seq, bounds, max_n=n_coords, time_remaining=end_time - time.time())\n        \n        # Apply smaller step of coordinate descent to new sequence\n        conv_val_new = np.convolve(new_seq, new_seq)\n        max_b_new = np.max(conv_val_new)\n        score_new = (2 * n_coords * max_b_new) / (np.sum(new_seq) ** 2) if np.sum(new_seq) > 0.01 else np.inf\n        \n        # Update best candidate\n        if score_new < best_score:\n            best_score = score_new\n            best_seq = new_seq\n        \n        # Check if improvement\n        if score_new < best_score_target:\n            print(f\"PROGRESS: Improved score from {best_score} to {score_new}\")\n            best_score = score_new\n            best_seq = new_seq\n            # Reschedule with updated parameters\n    \n    # Final fallback verification\n    if best_score >= 1.503:\n        fallback = [1.0] * 100\n        best_score = evaluate_sequence(fallback)\n        if best_score < np.inf and best_score < best_score:\n            best_seq = fallback.copy()\n            best_score = best_score\n    \n    print(f\"DONE: Final evaluation